summary: Linux Test Project
description: |
    LTP Introduction
    ================
    LTP is a famous test suite under Linux, I port LTP to Beaker every
    4 months (+/-1 month if needed). You can use this testcase for your
    RHEL testing.

    # Notes: SKIP_LEVEL is different to SKIPTESTS. SKIP_LEVEL is based on a script only
    to handle the known issues. And SKIPTESTS is used to skip general case in
    ltp/generic test suit.
contact: MM-QE <mm-qe@redhat.com>
id: c791670c-c33e-4cff-bc3f-3c92a5f94619
path: /distribution/ltp/generic
component:
  - kernel
  - glibc
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
require+:
  - procmail
  - automake
  - autoconf
  - flex
  - bison
  - rng-tools
  - rsyslog
  - util-linux
  - bc
  - gcc
  - bzip2
  - rpm-build
  - libaio-devel
  - libcap-devel
  - numactl-devel
  - numactl
  - strace
  - wget
  - python3
  - ntpsec
adjust+:
  - when: arch == x86_64
    enabled: false
duration: 180m
environment:
    TESTARGS: RHEL-TIME
extra-summary: /kernel/distribution/ltp/generic
extra-task: /kernel/distribution/ltp/generic
